{{/* @dot github.com/donseba/go-partial/examples/docs.DocsPage */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 text-[13px] font-extrabold uppercase text-emerald-300">Guide</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-5xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-slate-50">Rendering model</h1>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">A page is a partial tree. A wrapper partial can render a content child, registered regions keep stable IDs, and HTMX can request one target without losing the surrounding model.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Wrapper plus content</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The wrapper partial owns the page shell. The content partial owns the route-specific body. For a normal request, the wrapper renders the configured route partial with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ content }}" }}</code>. For an HTMX request, the connector can render only the requested target.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">blueprint := partial.NewID("shell", "shell.gohtml")
content := partial.NewID("content", "pages/dashboard.gohtml")

root := blueprint.Clone().SetContent(content)</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Registered regions</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Register regions in Go when they need a stable ID for wrapper composition, out-of-band rendering, or HTMX target requests.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">content.With(partial.NewID("stats", "partials/stats.gohtml"))</code></pre>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">{{ "{{ template \"stats.gohtml\" .Stats }}" }}</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">For typed row and component composition, prefer Go's native <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">template</code> action with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">@dot</code>. Register partials in Go when those templates also need stable HTMX target IDs.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Slots</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/slots</code> when a child region should render through its own partial lifecycle. A slot inherits the parent render stage chain, can participate in out-of-band updates, and appears as a child render in metrics. It is not a replacement for every native <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">template</code> call; it is for structured child partials.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">slots.Set(wrapper, "header", headerPartial)

{{ "{{ slot \"header\" }}" }}</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Request rendering flow</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>The route creates the content partial and any registered regions needed for that request.</li>
        <li>The reusable root partial carries shared configuration: filesystem, connector, function map, diagnostic events, cache, and render stage chain.</li>
        <li>The connector decides whether this is a full render or a partial render.</li>
        <li>For a full render, the wrapper renders the page shell and calls the configured content partial.</li>
        <li>For a partial render, go-partial renders the requested target and appends any out-of-band ancestors that should update too.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Request context</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">HTTP handlers should pass <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">r.Context()</code>, or a context derived from it, into <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.RenderWithRequest</code>. That is how cancellation, deadlines, localization, CSRF values, request event sinks, metrics IDs, and stage values travel through the render.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">ctx := metrics.WithRequestID(r.Context(), requestID)
ctx = partial.WithEventSink(ctx, requestEvents)

if err := partial.Write(ctx, w, r, content); err != nil {
    http.Error(w, "render failed", http.StatusInternalServerError)
    return
}</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Render(ctx, p)</code> is still useful for tests, offline rendering, and utilities that do not have an HTTP request. Request-aware helpers such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">request</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">url</code>, and connector values are naturally empty on that path.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Concurrency contract</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Already-configured root partials can be rendered concurrently after cloning. Configure them before serving requests, then treat methods such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetDot</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">With</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Use</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetFunc</code>, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetResponseHeaders</code> as configuration methods, not live request mutation.</p>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Per-render values are kept on the active render context. The request, URL, runtime object, selected target, helper bindings, stage values, and event sinks are not stored back onto reusable partials. When a route needs different dot data or children for each request, build that partial tree inside the handler.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Dynamic targets</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Use a target resolver when DOM IDs are dynamic, such as table rows. The resolver maps a browser target like <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">row-42</code> back to the row template and fresh dot data.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">target.WithResolver(table, func(ctx context.Context, r *http.Request, target string) (*partial.Partial, bool) {
    row := findRow(target)
    return partial.NewID(target, "partials/row.gohtml").SetDot(row), true
})</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><a href="/docs/target-resolver" hx-get="/docs/target-resolver" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">Read the full target resolver guide</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Render stage lifecycle</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Optional behavior uses the same render stage contract everywhere. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Prepare</code> sets up request-scoped context, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Render</code> wraps or replaces the terminal render, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Finalize</code> observes or transforms the result after success or failure.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">prepare A -&gt; prepare B
render A -&gt; render B -&gt; template render stage
finalize B -&gt; finalize A</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Writer APIs versus render APIs</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code> in HTTP handlers when possible. It owns response headers, protocol response instructions, error fragments, and out-of-band regions. Error output is provided by the optional <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">ext/errors</code> stage. Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.RenderWithRequest</code> when you want HTML and error handling under your own control.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Rendering a partial itself</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.RenderSelf(ctx, r, p)</code> renders the partial with the request, whatever target the request asks for, without out-of-band regions. Use it for HTML that reaches the browser another way, such as a server-sent event.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Rendering under a parent</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetParent(parent)</code> renders a partial under a configured partial without adding it to its children: it inherits the parent's functions, stages, connector, file system, template cache, failure policy and models, and the parent is not changed. One root can so be the parent of every component, e-mail or event an application renders on its own, without a clone per render.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">card := partial.NewID("card", "card.gohtml").SetDot(card).SetParent(root)
html, err := partial.RenderSelf(ctx, r, card)</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Rendering a defined template</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetEntry(name)</code> renders the template a file defines with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ define name }}" }}</code> instead of the file itself, for files with several parts, such as an e-mail with its subject, text and HTML.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">html, err := partial.Render(ctx, partial.New("mail/welcome.gohtml").SetEntry("html").SetDot(user))</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Unknown targets</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A partial request for a target the tree cannot resolve fails by default. A target fallback answers it with a partial of the tree instead, usually the content, rendered as if the client had asked for it, and tells the client to swap it where that partial lives.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.SetContent(content).
    SetTargetFallback(partial.TargetFallback{ID: "content", PushURL: true})</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Write</code> sends the retarget (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">#content</code>), the swap (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">outerHTML</code>) and, for GET requests, the URL to push through the connector: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Retarget</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Reswap</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Push-Url</code> for htmx. Set <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Retarget</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Swap</code> to change them.</p>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A slot of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/slots</code> that is requested on its own, such as a list that loads more rows, answers without the out-of-band regions of its parents with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">slots.OmitOOB()</code>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Templates from memory</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Sources</code> holds template sources in memory and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Overlay</code> looks files up in each layer in turn, so a package can ship default markup that applications replace with a file of their own. Partials, typed models and the template cache work as with any file system.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">var defaults = partial.Sources{
    "site/share.gohtml": `&lt;nav class="share"&gt;…&lt;/nav&gt;`,
}

share := partial.NewID("share", "site/share.gohtml").
    SetFileSystem(partial.Overlay(themeFiles, defaults))</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Create <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Sources</code> once, not per render: the template cache tells file systems apart by identity. Overlays are identified by their layers and may be built per render.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Vary</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code> adds the request headers the connector reads, such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Request</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target</code>, to the <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Vary</code> response header, so caches keep a page and a fragment of it apart.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Template cache</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">UseTemplateCache(true)</code> on the root turns the template cache on for the whole tree: children, content, the partials <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ partial }}" }}</code> renders and those rendered under the root with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetParent</code> use the setting of their nearest ancestor that sets one, unless they set it themselves.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.UseTemplateCache(!development)</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Shared includes</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetIncludes</code> gives every template of a partial and of the partials rendered under it the templates its <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">fs.Glob</code> patterns match, such as a theme's partials. Patterns resolve against the file system of the partial being rendered, a file is parsed once, and with the template cache a pattern is resolved once per file system.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root := partial.NewID("shell", "layout.gohtml").
    SetFileSystem(theme).
    SetIncludes("partials/*.gohtml")</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Data computed when needed</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.DotFuncOf</code>, set with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetDotSource</code>, computes a partial's dot only when the partial renders, on the page or as the target of a partial request, once per render tree. It keeps the type, so <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">CheckContracts</code> checks it against <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">@dot</code> without calling the function.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">stats := partial.DotFuncOf(func(ctx context.Context) (Stats, error) {
    return store.Stats(ctx)
})
panel := partial.NewID("stats", "stats.gohtml").SetDotSource(stats)</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Choosing a template</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">FirstExisting</code> returns the first of several templates that exists in a partial's file system, remembered per file system with the template cache; without a match the error wraps <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">fs.ErrNotExist</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">file, err := root.FirstExisting("pages/"+slug+".gohtml", "pages/"+kind+".gohtml", "pages/page.gohtml")</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Rendering text</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.RenderText(ctx, p)</code> renders with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">text/template</code>, for text that is not HTML, such as the subject and text part of an e-mail, with the file system, includes, functions, models, stages and cache of an HTML render. Nothing is escaped; stages see <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.RenderKindText</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">mail := partial.NewID("mail", "mail/welcome.gohtml").SetParent(root).SetDot(user)

subject, err := partial.RenderText(ctx, mail.SetEntry("subject"))
text, err := partial.RenderText(ctx, mail.SetEntry("text"))
html, err := partial.RenderSelf(ctx, nil, mail.SetEntry("html"))</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Content type</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Unless a header sets it, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code> sends <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8</code>.</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Child includes</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetChildIncludes</code> gives include patterns to the partials rendered under a partial only: a root gives its pages, regions, fragments and error templates the theme's partials without adding them to the parse of its layout. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">root.Glob(pattern)</code> returns the files a pattern matches, once per file system with the template cache.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.SetChildIncludes("partials/*.gohtml")</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Lazy models and dot values</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.ModelFuncOf(fn)</code> is a typed <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">@model</code> value computed only when a template calls it, once per render tree, also when the layout, header and sidebar each call it, which <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetModel</code> takes with other models. It is matched by its type, also by <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">CheckContracts</code>, without calling the function. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.DotFuncOf</code> makes a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Dot</code>, a dot that travels as a value, such as in a struct field, set with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetDotSource</code>. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetModel</code> ignores nil values.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.SetModel(partial.ModelFuncOf(func(ctx context.Context) (Navigation, error) {
    return loadNavigation(ctx)
}))

fragment := Fragment{ID: "stats", Dot: partial.DotFuncOf(loadStats)}
partial.NewID(fragment.ID, "stats.gohtml").SetDotSource(fragment.Dot)</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Choosing a template by layer</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Over <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Overlay(theme, defaults)</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">FirstExistingIn</code> tries every candidate in a layer before the next, so the theme's general template wins over the default specific one. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Defines(file, name)</code> reports whether a file defines a template and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HasEntry()</code> whether a partial's file defines its entry, from the scans renders use.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">file, err := root.FirstExistingIn(nil, "screens/"+key+".gohtml", "screens/"+kind+".gohtml")
ok, err := root.Defines("mail/welcome.gohtml", "html")</code></pre>
</article>

